# Use the image CMD (/entrypoint.sh) instead of replacing it with
# `sleep infinity`.
#
# /entrypoint.sh boots redis-server with the vulnerable config (bind 0.0.0.0,
# protected-mode no, no requirepass) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case detectable -
#     Redis reads redis.conf only at startup, so an unauthenticated PING still
#     returns PONG after a file-only edit;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting Redis cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART redis-server, not merely start
# it if absent - the daemon is already up with the vulnerable configuration.
